# R47 Track B — INDIRECT-DISPATCH CALL RESULT NEVER REGISTERED FOR DROP.
#
# CELL: arm = `Callable[T]` PARAMETER (its GIR local type is erased to unit,
# so the call lowers to the synthetic `__callable_N` indirect callee) ·
# position = discarded temp · payload = String · single call.
# Write site: `src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs`, the `UNIT_TYPE`-local arm.
#
# ⚠ WHY THE ARGUMENT IS A NAMED FUNCTION AND NOT A CLOSURE LITERAL. Passing
# `(): mk("hel","lo")` exercises the same arm, but it additionally allocates a
# closure environment through `__gorget_closure_env_alloc` — a DIFFERENT
# producer with its own 8-byte leak, known debt across ~77 corpus fixtures and
# explicitly out of this fixture's scope. `security_safe_no_leak` rejects ANY
# sanitizer output, so a closure-literal argument would leave this cell
# permanently un-wireable. A `FuncRef` argument isolates the call-result
# producer exactly.
#
# INSTRUMENT: `security_safe_no_leak`, C lane only (ASan is a no-op under
# `--backend=llvm`).
#
# RED-VERIFIED at pristine `f3feea79`: LEAK 6 byte(s) / 1 allocation, 3/3 runs.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

String maker():
    return mk("hel", "lo")

void call_it(Callable[String()] f):
    print(f())

void main():
    call_it(maker)
